UP-2 — route "preview-window-closed" to the launch that owns the window
===================================================================

SEVERITY: medium.  FILES: 3 (+1 new, +1 spec).

THE ISSUE
---------
GDevelop can open several preview windows at once (multi-window previews, and
the gameplay-test runner opening its own). Each launch registers its own
`onCaptureFinished` callback, and `PreviewWindow.js` closes by broadcasting a
message on the shared `preview-window-closed` channel — with NO information
about which window closed:

```js
// BEFORE — newIDE/electron-app/app/PreviewWindow.js
previewWindow.on('closed', () => {
  openEvent.sender.send('preview-window-closed');
});
```

On the renderer side the launcher compensated by removing ALL listeners and
re-registering its own on every launch:

```js
// BEFORE — LocalPreviewLauncher/index.js
ipcRenderer.removeAllListeners('preview-window-closed');
ipcRenderer.on('preview-window-closed', onPreviewWindowClosed);
```

That combination has two failure modes, both of them real:

1. **The surviving listener holds the wrong launch's state.** `removeAllListeners`
   wipes the other launch's handler, so after launching a second preview only
   the newest launch's `captureOptions` remain reachable. If the FIRST window
   closes, the second launch's `onCaptureFinished` runs — the wrong callback,
   with the wrong capture options. Screenshots can be attributed to the wrong
   run.
2. **A close for an unrelated window fires the callback.** Any preview window
   closing — including one opened by a completely different part of the app —
   triggers whichever listener is currently registered.

Neither is a crash, which is why it survived: it is a wrong-attribution bug
that shows up as "the capture finished early" or "a capture finished for a
preview I never took".

THE FIX
-------
Carry the window's identity in the message and route on it. Three parts:

1. **`PreviewWindow.js` reads the window id AT CREATION TIME and sends it.**
   This detail matters: by the time the `closed` event fires the window is
   already destroyed, so `previewWindow.id` inside the handler reads a
   destroyed object. The id has to be captured before that.

2. **`openPreviewWindow` returns the ids it created**, so the launcher can
   register them against the launch that opened them.

3. **`PreviewClosedTracker.js` (new, included in full in this package)** holds
   the window-id → capture-options map and routes a close to the right
   launch. The launcher then keeps ONE stable listener instead of tearing
   down and re-adding listeners per launch.

The tracker also swallows a rejection from `onCaptureFinished`. The caller
fires it from an IPC listener with `void`, so an async throw became an
unhandled rejection that could take the whole renderer down — and a failing
capture upload is exactly the kind of thing that throws. The window is gone
either way, so logging is the right behaviour.


DIFFS
-----
(1) newIDE/electron-app/app/PreviewWindow.js

```diff
   const createdWindowIds = [];
   ...
-      previewWindow.on('closed', () => {
+      // Read the id now: the window is destroyed when the "closed" event
+      // fires, so the id must not be read from `previewWindow` in its
+      // handler.
+      const windowId = previewWindow.id;
+      createdWindowIds.push(windowId);
+      previewWindow.on('closed', () => {
         ...
-        openEvent.sender.send('preview-window-closed');
+        // The closed window id is sent so that launchers can find the launch
+        // that owns the window (and its capture options).
+        openEvent.sender.send('preview-window-closed', windowId);
       });
   ...
+  return createdWindowIds;
```

(2) LocalPreviewLauncher/index.js — structural, summarised rather than
diffed inline because the file is large; the behavioural change is:

- `openPreviewWindow(...)` now yields the created window ids;
- after a successful launch, `previewClosedTracker.own(windowIds, captureOptions)`
  replaces re-registering a listener;
- a single `preview-window-closed` listener, registered once, calls
  `previewClosedTracker.handleClosed(windowId)`;
- on unmount, `previewClosedTracker.releaseAll()` instead of leaving a stale
  listener behind.

(3) PreviewClosedTracker.js — new file, full source included alongside this
patch.


COMPATIBILITY NOTE FOR REVIEWERS
---------------------------------
The IPC payload of `preview-window-closed` changes from no-argument to one
number. Any other listener on that channel will receive an argument it did not
expect. In this tree the only listeners are the launcher's, but if upstream has
others, they should tolerate an extra parameter. Nothing outside the preview
launcher subscribes to this channel.


TESTS
-----
`PreviewClosedTracker.spec.js` (included in this package) covers:
two launches, then closing the FIRST window's id — each launch's
`onCaptureFinished` fires exactly once for its OWN window and never for the
other's; double-close fires once; an unknown window id is ignored; a
re-launch replaces the mapping; multi-window launches are all tracked; and
`releaseAll` empties the map. A component-wiring spec asserts the launcher
actually registers the tracker.
